Basic Analysis of Temperature Sensitivity
Figure S4 illustrates that, despite achieving impressive R2 values of 0.999 during heating and
0.998 during cooling, these models are not robust across the full spectrum of temperature
variations. While they capture the general trend, they fall short in accurately representing
the gas detector’s signal response under dynamic temperature changes. This suggests that
simple linear regression models, though successful in controlled scenarios, fail to account for
the full complexity of the data, highlighting the need for more sophisticated approaches to
address the challenges posed by real-world environmental conditions.
