Impact Assessment of Gas Selectivity
As shown in Figure S6, CO2 concentrations below 500 ppm exert minimal influence on the
CH4 response ratio, indicating a relatively stable monitoring performance in environments
with moderate CO2 levels. However, when CO2 concentrations increase to 1000 ppm, a
noticeable rise in the CH4 response ratio is observed, suggesting that elevated CO2 lev
els enhance infrared absorption and may introduce significant measurement biases. While
fluctuations within ±500 ppm CO2 are unlikely to affect CH4 monitoring accuracy, larger
variations could compromise sensor reliability.
